============================================================

Authorization must work with Sprint 2 lifecycle.

Examples:

DELETED memory
→ cannot be read

ARCHIVED memory
→ access depends on architecture

EXPIRED memory
→ access depends on architecture

ACTIVE memory
→ normal policy evaluation

Do not duplicate lifecycle logic.

Use the existing lifecycle service/contracts.

============================================================
12. READ ENFORCEMENT
============================================================

Memory retrieval must require authorization.

No bypass.

Tests must verify:

authorized READ → succeeds

unauthorized READ → denied

wrong owner → denied

wrong scope → denied

insufficient security clearance → denied

deleted memory → denied

============================================================
13. WRITE ENFORCEMENT
============================================================

Memory creation must require authorization.

Tests:

authorized WRITE → succeeds

unauthorized WRITE → denied

wrong organization → denied

invalid agent group → denied

insufficient permission → denied

============================================================
14. UPDATE ENFORCEMENT
============================================================

Memory updates must require:

authorization

correct ownership/scope

valid lifecycle state

valid version

Tests must verify stale-version and unauthorized-update
combinations.

============================================================
15. DELETE ENFORCEMENT
============================================================

Deletion is highly sensitive.

Require explicit DELETE permission.

Do not treat UPDATE as DELETE.

Do not treat WRITE as DELETE.

Tests must verify:

WRITE only → DELETE denied

UPDATE only → DELETE denied

DELETE → allowed when all other policies pass

============================================================
16. ARCHIVE ENFORCEMENT
============================================================

Archive operations must require the appropriate permission.

Integrate with Sprint 2 lifecycle.

Do not bypass lifecycle validation.

